# Root-level environment configuration
# Each app manages its own .env — see apps/*/.env.example

# ── Cloudflare credentials ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required for any `wrangler` command that talks to Cloudflare (deploy, remote
# migrations, etc.). Two ways to provide them:
#
#   Option A — interactive login (persisted in ~/.wrangler/config):
#     wrangler login
#
#   Option B — env vars (useful for scripting or multiple accounts):
#     CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=   Your account ID (Cloudflare dashboard → right sidebar)
#     CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=    API token with "Workers Scripts: Edit" + "D1: Edit" permissions
#
# Local-only commands (wrangler dev, db:migrate:local) do NOT need these —
# they run against a local SQLite simulation with no network calls.

# ── GitHub Actions secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The same two variables above must also be set as repository secrets:
#   GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Repository secrets
#
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
